    "group": "Adult",
    "text": "- **Preferred:** \\*Piperacillin-tazobactam 4.5g IV q6–8h, 7 days OR Cefepime 2g IV q8h, 7 days\n- **Alternative (high MDR risk):** Meropenem 1g IV q8h, 7 days OR Imipenem/cilastatin 500mg IV q6h, 7 days\n- **Comments**\n  - See CAP section for pseudomonal risk.\n  - Severe pneumonia: septic shock; respiratory failure needing ventilatory support; rapid CXR progression.\n  - Empirical cover depends on local prevalence; de-escalate by culture and sensitivity.\n  - Longer duration may be indicated clinically/radiologically/biochemically.\n  - \\*Pip/tazo q8h: extended infusion over 3–4 hours."
