    "group": "Paediatric",
    "text": "- **Preferred:** Benzylpenicillin 200,000–300,000 units/kg/day IV in 4–6 divided doses (max. 24 million\n  units/day) PLUS Clindamycin 30–40mg/kg/day IV in 3–4 divided doses (max. 2.7g/day)\n- **Comments:** ~50% have streptococcal toxic shock syndrome. Prompt, aggressive surgical debridement\n  is the mainstay. Send tissue for Gram stain and culture. Clindamycin is needed in combination to block\n  toxin production whether or not toxic shock is present. IVIG adjunct in group A streptococcal\n  infection: 1g/kg Day 1, then 0.5g/kg on 1–2 subsequent days. Duration: at least 2 weeks if no focus\n  (no deep-seated, heart, bone or joint involvement)."
